From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:10:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: Live Text in the page's menu -- the text chosen
 translated, a scan read when asked, a PDF's page told to the room
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner, 2026-11-27: "build live text into spatimesh pdf viewer". SpatiLoupe's PDFs are SpatiMesh's
viewer's now; of SpatiLoupe's Live Text, choosing, copying and finding a page's text and a scan's (patch
0037) were there, and these come with it, on any page as well as in the PDF viewer:

- Translate, in the menu of text chosen: translated by the room's own model (hemera and its everyday
  model, from the room's AI settings) between the wearer's two languages -- text in the first into the
  second, anything else into the first, decided here from the model's word for the language, the lines
  numbered and put back where they were, digits kept: the questions of
  crates/spatiand-voice/src/hemera/translate.rs -- in a window of its own in the room's look:
  "Translating…", then "In <language>", the translation (to be chosen from), Copy and Done. The text is
  kept as the page gave it, lines and all: the menu's search item rewrites it before any command runs.
  Let out by the firewall under its own annotation (spatiand_translate).
- Read the text, with "read text in pictures by itself" off: a page whose pictures of text were left
  unread offers it; chosen, that page (by its address, in that tab) is read from then on and loaded
  again for it. The annotator is bound by frame, its tab remembering what was left unread.
- A full-page PDF's description for the room's assistant and dictation is its page most on show, by
  the PDF's own text (a scan's too, once read), not the viewer page's script-visible text, which holds
  none of it.
